# Security Guidelines

## Authentication & Authorization

### Role-Based Access Control
Two roles: `Administrator` and `User`

**User Model Methods**:
```php
$user->isAdministrator(); // Check if admin
$user->isActive();        // Check if account active
```

### AdminMiddleware
Protects admin routes:
```php
Route::middleware('admin')->group(function () {
    // Admin-only routes
});
```

**Checks**:
1. User is authenticated
2. User has Administrator role
3. User account is active

### Route Protection
```php
// Public routes - no middleware
Route::get('/products', [ProductCatalogController::class, 'index']);

// Authenticated routes
Route::middleware('auth')->group(function () {
    Route::get('/checkout', [CheckoutController::class, 'index']);
});

// Admin routes
Route::middleware(['auth', 'admin'])->group(function () {
    Route::get('/admin/dashboard', [DashboardController::class, 'index']);
});
```

## Input Validation

### Form Request Classes
Use for complex validation:
```php
class ProductRequest extends FormRequest
{
    public function rules()
    {
        return [
            'name' => 'required|string|max:255',
            'price' => 'required|numeric|min:0',
            'stock_quantity' => 'required|integer|min:0',
            'expiration_date' => 'required|date|after:today',
        ];
    }
    
    public function messages()
    {
        return [
            'name.required' => 'Tên sản phẩm là bắt buộc.',
            'price.min' => 'Giá phải lớn hơn hoặc bằng 0.',
        ];
    }
}
```

### Controller Validation
For simple cases:
```php
$validated = $request->validate([
    'email' => 'required|email',
    'password' => 'required|min:8',
]);
```

### Defense in Depth
Validate at multiple layers:
1. Client-side (user experience)
2. Controller (HTTP layer)
3. Service (business logic)
4. Database (constraints)

## Rate Limiting

### Login Throttling
```php
// In LoginRequest
RateLimiter::hit($this->throttleKey(), 60);

if (RateLimiter::tooManyAttempts($this->throttleKey(), 5)) {
    throw ValidationException::withMessages([
        'email' => 'Quá nhiều lần đăng nhập. Vui lòng thử lại sau 1 phút.',
    ]);
}
```

**Limits**: 5 attempts per minute per email

### Email Verification
```php
RateLimiter::attempt(
    'send-verification:'.$request->user()->id,
    6,
    function() { /* send email */ }
);
```

**Limits**: 6 attempts per minute per user

## Security Headers

### SecurityHeaders Middleware
Applied to all responses:
```php
X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
Content-Security-Policy: [detailed policy]
```

### CSP Configuration
Allows:
- Scripts: self, unsafe-inline, unsafe-eval, CDNs
- Styles: self, unsafe-inline, Google Fonts, CDNs
- Fonts: self, Google Fonts, CDNs
- Images: self, data:, https:, blob:
- Connections: self

## Database Security

### Parameterized Queries
Eloquent automatically uses prepared statements:
```php
// Safe - parameterized
Product::where('name', $userInput)->get();

// Unsafe - never do this
DB::select("SELECT * FROM products WHERE name = '$userInput'");
```

### Row Locking
Prevent race conditions:
```php
DB::transaction(function () {
    $product = Product::lockForUpdate()->find($id);
    $product->stock_quantity -= 1;
    $product->save();
});
```

### Soft Deletes
Preserve data integrity:
```php
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\SoftDeletes;

class Product extends Model
{
    use SoftDeletes;
}

// Soft delete
$product->delete(); // Sets deleted_at

// Restore
$product->restore();

// Permanent delete
$product->forceDelete();
```

## Password Security

### Hashing
Laravel uses bcrypt with 12 rounds:
```php
// Hash password
$hashed = Hash::make($password);

// Verify password
if (Hash::check($password, $hashed)) {
    // Correct
}
```

### Password Confirmation
Sensitive operations require re-confirmation:
```php
Route::middleware('password.confirm')->group(function () {
    Route::delete('/user', [UserController::class, 'destroy']);
});
```

**Timeout**: 3 hours (10800 seconds)

## Audit Logging

### Track All Admin Actions
AuditLogMiddleware logs:
- POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE requests
- On `/admin/*` routes
- User, IP, user agent, timestamp

### Track Model Changes
Auditable trait logs:
- Model creation
- Model updates (with old/new values)
- Model deletion

### Track Authentication
```php
AuditLogService::logAuthAttempt($email, $success, $reason);
AuditLogService::logLogout();
```

## Session Security

### Configuration
```php
'lifetime' => 120,              // 2 hours
'expire_on_close' => false,
'encrypt' => true,
'driver' => 'database',         // Persistent sessions
'secure' => env('SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE', true),
'http_only' => true,
'same_site' => 'lax',
```

### Session Regeneration
Regenerate on login to prevent fixation:
```php
$request->session()->regenerate();
```

## File Upload Security

### Validation
```php
$request->validate([
    'image' => 'required|image|mimes:jpeg,png,jpg|max:2048',
]);
```

### Storage
```php
$path = $request->file('image')->store('products', 'public');
```

**Never**:
- Execute uploaded files
- Trust file extensions
- Store in web-accessible directory without validation

## Best Practices Checklist

- [ ] Validate all user input
- [ ] Use Form Requests for complex validation
- [ ] Apply appropriate middleware to routes
- [ ] Implement rate limiting on sensitive endpoints
- [ ] Use transactions for multi-step operations
- [ ] Lock rows when modifying critical data
- [ ] Log all admin and sensitive operations
- [ ] Use soft deletes for data retention
- [ ] Hash passwords with bcrypt
- [ ] Regenerate sessions on login
- [ ] Set security headers on all responses
- [ ] Use HTTPS in production
- [ ] Keep dependencies updated
- [ ] Review audit logs regularly
